{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"pwd && sed -n '1,240p' TASK.md && sed -n '1,240p' definition.json && sed -n '1,280p' reference.py && sed -n '1,240p' workload.jsonl\"","aggregated_output":"/sgl-workspace/sol-execbench-rocm/artifacts/10/runs/full-01/codex/L2__071_edit_consistency_loss_with_perceptual_weighting/packet\n# Write the fastest correct kernel for `L2/071_edit_consistency_loss_with_perceptual_weighting`\n\nYou are optimizing one problem from SOL-ExecBench on an **AMD Instinct MI355X**\n(CDNA4, `gfx950`, 256 CUs, 288 GiB HBM3E). You have one GPU to yourself; it is\nalready the only one visible to you, so address it as `cuda:0`.\n\n## The problem\n\n`reference.py` defines the semantics. Your kernel must produce the same outputs\nfor every workload in `workload.jsonl`, within the tolerance each workload\nstates. `definition.json` describes the input shapes and dtypes, where the axes\nare symbolic (`batch_size`, `seq_len`, ...) and each workload binds them to\nconcrete values.\n\nRead all three files before writing anything. There are **16\nworkloads** and they cover a range of shapes; a kernel that only handles the\nfirst one is not a solution.\n\n## What you produce\n\nA single file `solution.json` in this directory. Nothing else is collected.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"071_edit_consistency_loss_with_perceptual_weighting_agent\",\n  \"definition\": \"071_edit_consistency_loss_with_perceptual_weighting\",\n  \"author\": \"agent\",\n  \"spec\": {\n    \"languages\": [\"triton\"],\n    \"target_hardware\": [\"MI355X\", \"LOCAL\"],\n    \"entry_point\": \"kernel.py::run\",\n    \"dependencies\": [\"torch\", \"triton\"],\n    \"destination_passing_style\": false\n  },\n  \"sources\": [\n    {\"path\": \"kernel.py\", \"content\": \"\"}\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nWrite your kernel to `kernel.py` as a real file and leave `content` as `\"\"` --\nthe loader fills it in from `path`. You may also inline the content instead if\nyou prefer; both work. Multiple source files are fine.\n\n**Write `solution.json` before you start iterating, not at the end.** Only that\nfile is collected, and a session can end without warning -- a wallclock cap, or\nthe API gateway dropping the connection. If that happens with no\n`solution.json` on disk, a working kernel scores exactly the same as no kernel\nat all. Write it as soon as you have a first attempt, then keep improving\n`kernel.py` in place; the loader re-reads the file each time you verify, so you\ndo not need to touch `solution.json` again.\n\nThe entry point function must accept the inputs in the order\n`definition.json` lists them and **return** the outputs (that is what\n`destination_passing_style: false` means). Match `reference.py`'s signature.\n\n## Languages\n\nAny of these. You are not restricted to one, and you are not expected to use\nthe most exotic one that fits -- use whatever actually gets the speed.\n\n| `spec.languages` value | What it is | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `pytorch` | plain torch ops, `torch.compile` allowed | the baseline; correct but rarely fast |\n| `triton` | Triton JIT kernels | the usual first choice on ROCm |\n| `triton` + Gluon | `triton.experimental.gluon` | lower-level tile/layout control, same `triton` language value |\n| `hip_cpp` | HIP C++, compiled `--offload-arch=gfx950` | inline GCN assembly via `asm volatile` lives here |\n| `ck` / `ck_tile` | AMD Composable Kernel | headers under `/opt/rocm/include` |\n| `hipblaslt` | AMD hipBLASLt | GEMM with epilogue fusion |\n| `miopen` | AMD MIOpen | convolutions |\n| `aiter` | AMD AI Tensor Engine for ROCm | prebuilt fused kernels |\n\n\nC++ and Python languages cannot be mixed in one solution. For `hip_cpp`, source\nfiles use `.hip` or `.cpp`; `--offload-arch=gfx950` is injected for you.\n\n## Verifying\n\n```bash\n./verify\n```\n\nCompiles and evaluates your current `solution.json` against every workload on\nreal hardware and prints, per workload: pass/fail, the measured error against\nthe allowed tolerance, and your latency beside the reference's.\n\n**You may run it 5 times.** Attempt counts are tracked for you and each run tells you how many remain. Use them:\na kernel that has never been executed is usually wrong. But do read the\nreference carefully first rather than spending attempts on guesses -- the most\ncommon failure here is not a slow kernel, it is a kernel that gets the\nnumerics subtly wrong.\n\n`./verify` is your feedback, not your score. Your solution is re-evaluated\nafterwards from a clean tree on a different GPU, and that run is what counts.\n\n## How you are scored\n\n1. **Correctness first.** A wrong kernel scores nothing regardless of speed.\n   All 16 workloads must pass.\n2. **Then speed**, as proximity to an analytically derived Speed-of-Light bound\n   for this hardware -- not as speedup over PyTorch. Being 2x faster than the\n   reference is worth little if the hardware bound is 10x away; getting close\n   to the bound is worth a lot.\n\nSo: match the numerics exactly, then remove memory traffic and launch overhead.\nFusing the reference's separate operations into one pass over the data is\nusually where the win is.\n\n## Numerics, specifically\n\nThe reference's *order of operations* is part of the specification. Reproduce\nits intermediate rounding, not just its algebra: if it rounds a `float32`\naccumulator to `bfloat16` before a multiply, so must you, or you will be more\naccurate than the reference and still fail the tolerance. Accumulate in\n`float32` where the reference does.\n\n## Not allowed\n\nThe harness detects all of these and a solution caught by any of them scores\nzero:\n\n- Monkey-patching torch, the harness, or the timing path.\n- Caching outputs across calls, or returning a lazily-evaluated handle so the\n  work lands outside the timed region.\n- Touching GPU clocks, `rocm-smi`, or `amd-smi`.\n- Editing anything outside this directory.\n- Special-casing the specific input values or workload shapes to skip work that\n  the semantics require.\n\nMaking the kernel genuinely faster is the whole exercise. Everything above is a\nway of appearing faster instead, and is checked for.\n{\n  \"name\": \"071_edit_consistency_loss_with_perceptual_weighting\",\n  \"description\": \"Edit consistency loss combining pixel reconstruction, perceptual features, and edit-region-aware spatial weighting for image editing models. Computes multi-scale perceptual features, applies spatial weighting based on edit masks, and combines pixel loss, perceptual loss, and preservation loss.\",\n  \"hf_id\": \"stepfun-ai/Step1X-Edit-v1p2\",\n  \"custom_inputs_entrypoint\": \"get_inputs\",\n  \"axes\": {\n    \"batch_size\": {\n      \"type\": \"var\",\n      \"description\": \"Batch size\"\n    },\n    \"height\": {\n      \"type\": \"var\",\n      \"description\": \"Image height\"\n    },\n    \"width\": {\n      \"type\": \"var\",\n      \"description\": \"Image width\"\n    },\n    \"channels\": {\n      \"type\": \"const\",\n      \"value\": 3,\n      \"description\": \"Image channels (RGB)\"\n    },\n    \"feat_dim_0\": {\n      \"type\": \"const\",\n      \"value\": 64,\n      \"description\": \"First perceptual feature dimension\"\n    },\n    \"feat_dim_1\": {\n      \"type\": \"const\",\n      \"value\": 128,\n      \"description\": \"Second perceptual feature dimension\"\n    },\n    \"feat_dim_2\": {\n      \"type\": \"const\",\n      \"value\": 256,\n      \"description\": \"Third perceptual feature dimension\"\n    },\n    \"num_scales\": {\n      \"type\": \"const\",\n      \"value\": 3,\n      \"description\": \"Number of perceptual scales\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"inputs\": {\n    \"predicted\": {\n      \"shape\": [\n        \"batch_size\",\n        \"channels\",\n        \"height\",\n        \"width\"\n      ],\n      \"dtype\": \"float32\",\n      \"description\": \"Predicted edited image\"\n    },\n    \"target\": {\n      \"shape\": [\n        \"batch_size\",\n        \"channels\",\n        \"height\",\n        \"width\"\n      ],\n      \"dtype\": \"float32\",\n      \"description\": \"Target edited image\"\n    },\n    \"source\": {\n      \"shape\": [\n        \"batch_size\",\n        \"channels\",\n        \"height\",\n        \"width\"\n      ],\n      \"dtype\": \"float32\",\n      \"description\": \"Source image before editing\"\n    },\n    \"edit_mask\": {\n      \"shape\": [\n        \"batch_size\",\n        \"1\",\n        \"height\",\n        \"width\"\n      ],\n      \"dtype\": \"float32\",\n      \"description\": \"Binary mask indicating edit regions (1.0=edited, 0.0=preserved)\"\n    },\n    \"extractor0_conv1_weight\": {\n      \"shape\": [\n        \"feat_dim_0\",\n        \"channels\",\n        \"3\",\n        \"3\"\n      ],\n      \"dtype\": \"float32\",\n      \"description\": \"First extractor conv1 weight\"\n    },\n    \"extractor0_conv1_bias\": {\n      \"shape\": [\n        \"feat_dim_0\"\n      ],\n      \"dtype\": \"float32\",\n      \"description\": \"First extractor conv1 bias\"\n    },\n    \"extractor0_conv2_weight\": {\n      \"shape\": [\n        \"feat_dim_0\",\n        \"feat_dim_0\",\n        \"3\",\n        \"3\"\n      ],\n      \"dtype\": \"float32\",\n      \"description\": \"First extractor conv2 weight\"\n    },\n    \"extractor0_conv2_bias\": {\n      \"shape\": [\n        \"feat_dim_0\"\n      ],\n      \"dtype\": \"float32\",\n      \"description\": \"First extractor conv2 bias\"\n    },\n    \"extractor1_conv1_weight\": {\n      \"shape\": [\n        \"feat_dim_1\",\n        \"feat_dim_0\",\n        \"3\",\n        \"3\"\n      ],\n      \"dtype\": \"float32\",\n      \"description\": \"Second extractor conv1 weight\"\n    },\n    \"extractor1_conv1_bias\": {\n      \"shape\": [\n        \"feat_dim_1\"\n      ],\n      \"dtype\": \"float32\",\n      \"description\": \"Second extractor conv1 bias\"\n    },\n    \"extractor1_conv2_weight\": {\n      \"shape\": [\n        \"feat_dim_1\",\n        \"feat_dim_1\",\n        \"3\",\n        \"3\"\n      ],\n      \"dtype\": \"float32\",\n      \"description\": \"Second extractor conv2 weight\"\n    },\n    \"extractor1_conv2_bias\": {\n      \"shape\": [\n        \"feat_dim_1\"\n      ],\n      \"dtype\": \"float32\",\n      \"description\": \"Second extractor conv2 bias\"\n    },\n    \"extractor2_conv1_weight\": {\n      \"shape\": [\n        \"feat_dim_2\",\n        \"feat_dim_1\",\n        \"3\",\n        \"3\"\n      ],\n      \"dtype\": \"float32\",\n      \"description\": \"Third extractor conv1 weight\"\n    },\n    \"extractor2_conv1_bias\": {\n      \"shape\": [\n        \"feat_dim_2\"\n      ],\n      \"dtype\": \"float32\",\n      \"description\": \"Third extractor conv1 bias\"\n    },\n    \"extractor2_conv2_weight\": {\n      \"shape\": [\n        \"feat_dim_2\",\n        \"feat_dim_2\",\n        \"3\",\n        \"3\"\n      ],\n      \"dtype\": \"float32\",\n      \"description\": \"Third extractor conv2 weight\"\n    },\n    \"extractor2_conv2_bias\": {\n      \"shape\": [\n        \"feat_dim_2\"\n      ],\n      \"dtype\": \"float32\",\n      \"description\": \"Third extractor conv2 bias\"\n    },\n    \"scale_weights\": {\n      \"shape\": [\n        \"num_scales\"\n      ],\n      \"dtype\": \"float32\",\n      \"description\": \"Learnable per-scale perceptual loss weights\"\n    },\n    \"pixel_loss_weight\": {\n      \"shape\": null,\n      \"dtype\": \"float32\",\n      \"description\": \"Weight for pixel loss term\"\n    },\n    \"perceptual_loss_weight\": {\n      \"shape\": null,\n      \"dtype\": \"float32\",\n      \"description\": \"Weight for perceptual loss term\"\n    },\n    \"edit_region_weight_multiplier\": {\n      \"shape\": null,\n      \"dtype\": \"float32\",\n      \"description\": \"Multiplier for edit region weights\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"outputs\": {\n    \"total_loss\": {\n      \"shape\": [],\n      \"dtype\": \"float32\",\n      \"description\": \"Total weighted loss value\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"reference\": \"import torch\\nimport torch.nn.functional as F\\n\\n\\ndef get_inputs(\\n    axes_and_scalars: dict, device: torch.device\\n) -> dict:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Generate inputs for the edit consistency loss.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    batch_size = axes_and_scalars[\\\"batch_size\\\"]\\n    height = axes_and_scalars[\\\"height\\\"]\\n    width = axes_and_scalars[\\\"width\\\"]\\n    channels = 3\\n    feat_dim_0 = 64\\n    feat_dim_1 = 128\\n    feat_dim_2 = 256\\n    num_scales = 3\\n    \\n    # Image tensors\\n    predicted = torch.randn(batch_size, channels, height, width, dtype=torch.float32, device=device)\\n    target = torch.randn(batch_size, channels, height, width, dtype=torch.float32, device=device)\\n    source = torch.randn(batch_size, channels, height, width, dtype=torch.float32, device=device)\\n    \\n    # Edit mask - binary values\\n    edit_mask = (torch.rand(batch_size, 1, height, width, device=device) > 0.5).float()\\n    \\n    # Extractor weights with proper initialization\\n    extractor0_conv1_weight = torch.randn(feat_dim_0, channels, 3, 3, dtype=torch.float32, device=device) * 0.1\\n    extractor0_conv1_bias = torch.zeros(feat_dim_0, dtype=torch.float32, device=device)\\n    extractor0_conv2_weight = torch.randn(feat_dim_0, feat_dim_0, 3, 3, dtype=torch.float32, device=device) * 0.1\\n    extractor0_conv2_bias = torch.zeros(feat_dim_0, dtype=torch.float32, device=device)\\n    \\n    extractor1_conv1_weight = torch.randn(feat_dim_1, feat_dim_0, 3, 3, dtype=torch.float32, device=device) * 0.1\\n    extractor1_conv1_bias = torch.zeros(feat_dim_1, dtype=torch.float32, device=device)\\n    extractor1_conv2_weight = torch.randn(feat_dim_1, feat_dim_1, 3, 3, dtype=torch.float32, device=device) * 0.1\\n    extractor1_conv2_bias = torch.zeros(feat_dim_1, dtype=torch.float32, device=device)\\n    \\n    extractor2_conv1_weight = torch.randn(feat_dim_2, feat_dim_1, 3, 3, dtype=torch.float32, device=device) * 0.1\\n    extractor2_conv1_bias = torch.zeros(feat_dim_2, dtype=torch.float32, device=device)\\n    extractor2_conv2_weight = torch.randn(feat_dim_2, feat_dim_2, 3, 3, dtype=torch.float32, device=device) * 0.1\\n    extractor2_conv2_bias = torch.zeros(feat_dim_2, dtype=torch.float32, device=device)\\n    \\n    # Scale weights\\n    scale_weights = torch.ones(num_scales, dtype=torch.float32, device=device) / num_scales\\n    \\n    # Scalar values\\n    pixel_loss_weight = 1.0\\n    perceptual_loss_weight = 0.5\\n    edit_region_weight_multiplier = 2.0\\n    \\n    return {\\n        \\\"predicted\\\": predicted,\\n        \\\"target\\\": target,\\n        \\\"source\\\": source,\\n        \\\"edit_mask\\\": edit_mask,\\n        \\\"extractor0_conv1_weight\\\": extractor0_conv1_weight,\\n        \\\"extractor0_conv1_bias\\\": extractor0_conv1_bias,\\n        \\\"extractor0_conv2_weight\\\": extractor0_conv2_weight,\\n        \\\"extractor0_conv2_bias\\\": extractor0_conv2_bias,\\n        \\\"extractor1_conv1_weight\\\": extractor1_conv1_weight,\\n        \\\"extractor1_conv1_bias\\\": extractor1_conv1_bias,\\n        \\\"extractor1_conv2_weight\\\": extractor1_conv2_weight,\\n        \\\"extractor1_conv2_bias\\\": extractor1_conv2_bias,\\n        \\\"extractor2_conv1_weight\\\": extractor2_conv1_weight,\\n        \\\"extractor2_conv1_bias\\\": extractor2_conv1_bias,\\n        \\\"extractor2_conv2_weight\\\": extractor2_conv2_weight,\\n        \\\"extractor2_conv2_bias\\\": extractor2_conv2_bias,\\n        \\\"scale_weights\\\": scale_weights,\\n        \\\"pixel_loss_weight\\\": pixel_loss_weight,\\n        \\\"perceptual_loss_weight\\\": perceptual_loss_weight,\\n        \\\"edit_region_weight_multiplier\\\": edit_region_weight_multiplier,\\n    }\\n\\n\\n@torch.no_grad()\\ndef run(\\n    predicted: torch.Tensor,\\n    target: torch.Tensor,\\n    source: torch.Tensor,\\n    edit_mask: torch.Tensor,\\n    extractor0_conv1_weight: torch.Tensor,\\n    extractor0_conv1_bias: torch.Tensor,\\n    extractor0_conv2_weight: torch.Tensor,\\n    extractor0_conv2_bias: torch.Tensor,\\n    extractor1_conv1_weight: torch.Tensor,\\n    extractor1_conv1_bias: torch.Tensor,\\n    extractor1_conv2_weight: torch.Tensor,\\n    extractor1_conv2_bias: torch.Tensor,\\n    extractor2_conv1_weight: torch.Tensor,\\n    extractor2_conv1_bias: torch.Tensor,\\n    extractor2_conv2_weight: torch.Tensor,\\n    extractor2_conv2_bias: torch.Tensor,\\n    scale_weights: torch.Tensor,\\n    pixel_loss_weight: float,\\n    perceptual_loss_weight: float,\\n    edit_region_weight_multiplier: float,\\n):\\n    # Sobel kernels for edge detection\\n    sobel_x = torch.tensor([[-1, 0, 1], [-2, 0, 2], [-1, 0, 1]], dtype=torch.float32, device=edit_mask.device).view(1, 1, 3, 3)\\n    sobel_y = torch.tensor([[-1, -2, -1], [0, 0, 0], [1, 2, 1]], dtype=torch.float32, device=edit_mask.device).view(1, 1, 3, 3)\\n    \\n    # Compute edge map from edit mask\\n    edges_x = F.conv2d(edit_mask, sobel_x, padding=1)\\n    edges_y = F.conv2d(edit_mask, sobel_y, padding=1)\\n    edge_magnitude = torch.sqrt(edges_x ** 2 + edges_y ** 2 + 1e-8)\\n    \\n    # Compute spatial weights\\n    spatial_weights = torch.ones_like(edit_mask)\\n    spatial_weights = spatial_weights + (edit_region_weight_multiplier - 1.0) * edit_mask\\n    spatial_weights = spatial_weights + 0.5 * edge_magnitude\\n    \\n    # 1. Pixel-level reconstruction loss (L1)\\n    pixel_diff = torch.abs(predicted - target)\\n    weighted_pixel_loss = pixel_diff * spatial_weights\\n    pixel_loss = weighted_pixel_loss.mean()\\n    \\n    # 2. Extract perceptual features for predicted and target\\n    def extract_features(x, conv1_w, conv1_b, conv2_w, conv2_b):\\n        x = F.conv2d(x, conv1_w, conv1_b, padding=1)\\n        x = F.relu(x)\\n        x = F.conv2d(x, conv2_w, conv2_b, padding=1)\\n        x = F.relu(x)\\n        x = F.max_pool2d(x, kernel_size=2, stride=2)\\n        return x\\n    \\n    # Scale 0\\n    pred_feat0 = extract_features(predicted, extractor0_conv1_weight, extractor0_conv1_bias, extractor0_conv2_weight, extractor0_conv2_bias)\\n    target_feat0 = extract_features(target, extractor0_conv1_weight, extractor0_conv1_bias, extractor0_conv2_weight, extractor0_conv2_bias)\\n    \\n    # Scale 1\\n    pred_feat1 = extract_features(pred_feat0, extractor1_conv1_weight, extractor1_conv1_bias, extractor1_conv2_weight, extractor1_conv2_bias)\\n    target_feat1 = extract_features(target_feat0, extractor1_conv1_weight, extractor1_conv1_bias, extractor1_conv2_weight, extractor1_conv2_bias)\\n    \\n    # Scale 2\\n    pred_feat2 = extract_features(pred_feat1, extractor2_conv1_weight, extractor2_conv1_bias, extractor2_conv2_weight, extractor2_conv2_bias)\\n    target_feat2 = extract_features(target_feat1, extractor2_conv1_weight, extractor2_conv1_bias, extractor2_conv2_weight, extractor2_conv2_bias)\\n    \\n    pred_features = [pred_feat0, pred_feat1, pred_feat2]\\n    target_features = [target_feat0, target_feat1, target_feat2]\\n    \\n    # Compute perceptual loss across scales\\n    perceptual_loss = torch.tensor(0.0, dtype=torch.float32, device=predicted.device)\\n    \\n    for scale_idx in range(3):\\n        pred_feat = pred_features[scale_idx]\\n        target_feat = target_features[scale_idx]\\n        \\n        # Downsample spatial weights to match feature resolution\\n        downsampled_weights = F.interpolate(\\n            spatial_weights,\\n            size=(pred_feat.shape[2], pred_feat.shape[3]),\\n            mode='bilinear',\\n            align_corners=False\\n        )\\n        \\n        # Compute weighted perceptual difference\\n        feat_diff = torch.abs(pred_feat - target_feat)\\n        weighted_feat_diff = feat_diff * downsampled_weights\\n        scale_loss = weighted_feat_diff.mean()\\n        \\n        # Apply learnable scale weight\\n        scale_loss = scale_loss * torch.abs(scale_weights[scale_idx])\\n        perceptual_loss = perceptual_loss + scale_loss\\n    \\n    # 3. Preservation loss for non-edited regions\\n    inverse_mask = 1.0 - edit_mask\\n    preservation_diff = torch.abs(predicted - source) * inverse_mask\\n    preservation_loss = preservation_diff.mean()\\n    \\n    # Combine all losses\\n    total_loss = (\\n        pixel_loss_weight * pixel_loss +\\n        perceptual_loss_weight * perceptual_loss +\\n        0.3 * preservation_loss\\n    )\\n    \\n    return total_loss\\n\"\n}\nimport torch\nimport torch.nn.functional as F\n\n\ndef get_inputs(\n    axes_and_scalars: dict, device: torch.device\n) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"Generate inputs for the edit consistency loss.\"\"\"\n    batch_size = axes_and_scalars[\"batch_size\"]\n    height = axes_and_scalars[\"height\"]\n    width = axes_and_scalars[\"width\"]\n    channels = 3\n    feat_dim_0 = 64\n    feat_dim_1 = 128\n    feat_dim_2 = 256\n    num_scales = 3\n    \n    # Image tensors\n    predicted = torch.randn(batch_size, channels, height, width, dtype=torch.float32, device=device)\n    target = torch.randn(batch_size, channels, height, width, dtype=torch.float32, device=device)\n    source = torch.randn(batch_size, channels, height, width, dtype=torch.float32, device=device)\n    \n    # Edit mask - binary values\n    edit_mask = (torch.rand(batch_size, 1, height, width, device=device) > 0.5).float()\n    \n    # Extractor weights with proper initialization\n    extractor0_conv1_weight = torch.randn(feat_dim_0, channels, 3, 3, dtype=torch.float32, device=device) * 0.1\n    extractor0_conv1_bias = torch.zeros(feat_dim_0, dtype=torch.float32, device=device)\n    extractor0_conv2_weight = torch.randn(feat_dim_0, feat_dim_0, 3, 3, dtype=torch.float32, device=device) * 0.1\n    extractor0_conv2_bias = torch.zeros(feat_dim_0, dtype=torch.float32, device=device)\n    \n    extractor1_conv1_weight = torch.randn(feat_dim_1, feat_dim_0, 3, 3, dtype=torch.float32, device=device) * 0.1\n    extractor1_conv1_bias = torch.zeros(feat_dim_1, dtype=torch.float32, device=device)\n    extractor1_conv2_weight = torch.randn(feat_dim_1, feat_dim_1, 3, 3, dtype=torch.float32, device=device) * 0.1\n    extractor1_conv2_bias = torch.zeros(feat_dim_1, dtype=torch.float32, device=device)\n    \n    extractor2_conv1_weight = torch.randn(feat_dim_2, feat_dim_1, 3, 3, dtype=torch.float32, device=device) * 0.1\n    extractor2_conv1_bias = torch.zeros(feat_dim_2, dtype=torch.float32, device=device)\n    extractor2_conv2_weight = torch.randn(feat_dim_2, feat_dim_2, 3, 3, dtype=torch.float32, device=device) * 0.1\n    extractor2_conv2_bias = torch.zeros(feat_dim_2, dtype=torch.float32, device=device)\n    \n    # Scale weights\n    scale_weights = torch.ones(num_scales, dtype=torch.float32, device=device) / num_scales\n    \n    # Scalar values\n    pixel_loss_weight = 1.0\n    perceptual_loss_weight = 0.5\n    edit_region_weight_multiplier = 2.0\n    \n    return {\n        \"predicted\": predicted,\n        \"target\": target,\n        \"source\": source,\n        \"edit_mask\": edit_mask,\n        \"extractor0_conv1_weight\": extractor0_conv1_weight,\n        \"extractor0_conv1_bias\": extractor0_conv1_bias,\n        \"extractor0_conv2_weight\": extractor0_conv2_weight,\n        \"extractor0_conv2_bias\": extractor0_conv2_bias,\n        \"extractor1_conv1_weight\": extractor1_conv1_weight,\n        \"extractor1_conv1_bias\": extractor1_conv1_bias,\n        \"extractor1_conv2_weight\": extractor1_conv2_weight,\n        \"extractor1_conv2_bias\": extractor1_conv2_bias,\n        \"extractor2_conv1_weight\": extractor2_conv1_weight,\n        \"extractor2_conv1_bias\": extractor2_conv1_bias,\n        \"extractor2_conv2_weight\": extractor2_conv2_weight,\n        \"extractor2_conv2_bias\": extractor2_conv2_bias,\n        \"scale_weights\": scale_weights,\n        \"pixel_loss_weight\": pixel_loss_weight,\n        \"perceptual_loss_weight\": perceptual_loss_weight,\n        \"edit_region_weight_multiplier\": edit_region_weight_multiplier,\n    }\n\n\n@torch.no_grad()\ndef run(\n    predicted: torch.Tensor,\n    target: torch.Tensor,\n    source: torch.Tensor,\n    edit_mask: torch.Tensor,\n    extractor0_conv1_weight: torch.Tensor,\n    extractor0_conv1_bias: torch.Tensor,\n    extractor0_conv2_weight: torch.Tensor,\n    extractor0_conv2_bias: torch.Tensor,\n    extractor1_conv1_weight: torch.Tensor,\n    extractor1_conv1_bias: torch.Tensor,\n    extractor1_conv2_weight: torch.Tensor,\n    extractor1_conv2_bias: torch.Tensor,\n    extractor2_conv1_weight: torch.Tensor,\n    extractor2_conv1_bias: torch.Tensor,\n    extractor2_conv2_weight: torch.Tensor,\n    extractor2_conv2_bias: torch.Tensor,\n    scale_weights: torch.Tensor,\n    pixel_loss_weight: float,\n    perceptual_loss_weight: float,\n    edit_region_weight_multiplier: float,\n):\n    # Sobel kernels for edge detection\n    sobel_x = torch.tensor([[-1, 0, 1], [-2, 0, 2], [-1, 0, 1]], dtype=torch.float32, device=edit_mask.device).view(1, 1, 3, 3)\n    sobel_y = torch.tensor([[-1, -2, -1], [0, 0, 0], [1, 2, 1]], dtype=torch.float32, device=edit_mask.device).view(1, 1, 3, 3)\n    \n    # Compute edge map from edit mask\n    edges_x = F.conv2d(edit_mask, sobel_x, padding=1)\n    edges_y = F.conv2d(edit_mask, sobel_y, padding=1)\n    edge_magnitude = torch.sqrt(edges_x ** 2 + edges_y ** 2 + 1e-8)\n    \n    # Compute spatial weights\n    spatial_weights = torch.ones_like(edit_mask)\n    spatial_weights = spatial_weights + (edit_region_weight_multiplier - 1.0) * edit_mask\n    spatial_weights = spatial_weights + 0.5 * edge_magnitude\n    \n    # 1. Pixel-level reconstruction loss (L1)\n    pixel_diff = torch.abs(predicted - target)\n    weighted_pixel_loss = pixel_diff * spatial_weights\n    pixel_loss = weighted_pixel_loss.mean()\n    \n    # 2. Extract perceptual features for predicted and target\n    def extract_features(x, conv1_w, conv1_b, conv2_w, conv2_b):\n        x = F.conv2d(x, conv1_w, conv1_b, padding=1)\n        x = F.relu(x)\n        x = F.conv2d(x, conv2_w, conv2_b, padding=1)\n        x = F.relu(x)\n        x = F.max_pool2d(x, kernel_size=2, stride=2)\n        return x\n    \n    # Scale 0\n    pred_feat0 = extract_features(predicted, extractor0_conv1_weight, extractor0_conv1_bias, extractor0_conv2_weight, extractor0_conv2_bias)\n    target_feat0 = extract_features(target, extractor0_conv1_weight, extractor0_conv1_bias, extractor0_conv2_weight, extractor0_conv2_bias)\n    \n    # Scale 1\n    pred_feat1 = extract_features(pred_feat0, extractor1_conv1_weight, extractor1_conv1_bias, extractor1_conv2_weight, extractor1_conv2_bias)\n    target_feat1 = extract_features(target_feat0, extractor1_conv1_weight, extractor1_conv1_bias, extractor1_conv2_weight, extractor1_conv2_bias)\n    \n    # Scale 2\n    pred_feat2 = extract_features(pred_feat1, extractor2_conv1_weight, extractor2_conv1_bias, extractor2_conv2_weight, extractor2_conv2_bias)\n    target_feat2 = extract_features(target_feat1, extractor2_conv1_weight, extractor2_conv1_bias, extractor2_conv2_weight, extractor2_conv2_bias)\n    \n    pred_features = [pred_feat0, pred_feat1, pred_feat2]\n    target_features = [target_feat0, target_feat1, target_feat2]\n    \n    # Compute perceptual loss across scales\n    perceptual_loss = torch.tensor(0.0, dtype=torch.float32, device=predicted.device)\n    \n    for scale_idx in range(3):\n        pred_feat = pred_features[scale_idx]\n        target_feat = target_features[scale_idx]\n        \n        # Downsample spatial weights to match feature resolution\n        downsampled_weights = F.interpolate(\n            spatial_weights,\n            size=(pred_feat.shape[2], pred_feat.shape[3]),\n            mode='bilinear',\n            align_corners=False\n        )\n        \n        # Compute weighted perceptual difference\n        feat_diff = torch.abs(pred_feat - target_feat)\n        weighted_feat_diff = feat_diff * downsampled_weights\n        scale_loss = weighted_feat_diff.mean()\n        \n        # Apply learnable scale weight\n        scale_loss = scale_loss * torch.abs(scale_weights[scale_idx])\n        perceptual_loss = perceptual_loss + scale_loss\n    \n    # 3. Preservation loss for non-edited regions\n    inverse_mask = 1.0 - edit_mask\n    preservation_diff = torch.abs(predicted - source) * inverse_mask\n    preservation_loss = preservation_diff.mean()\n    \n    # Combine all losses\n    total_loss = (\n        pixel_loss_weight * pixel_loss +\n        perceptual_loss_weight * perceptual_loss +\n        0.3 * preservation_loss\n    )\n    \n    return total_loss\n{\"uuid\": \"f723e0d9-a85f-5c45-8f7e-779b7a609d3b\", \"axes\": {\"batch_size\": 1, \"height\": 1024, \"width\": 1024}, \"inputs\": {\"predicted\": {\"type\": \"custom\"}, \"target\": {\"type\": \"custom\"}, \"source\": {\"type\": \"custom\"}, \"edit_mask\": {\"type\": \"custom\"}, \"extractor0_conv1_weight\": {\"type\": \"custom\"}, \"extractor0_conv1_bias\": {\"type\": \"custom\"}, \"extractor0_conv2_weight\": {\"type\": \"custom\"}, \"extractor0_conv2_bias\": {\"type\": \"custom\"}, \"extractor1_conv1_weight\": {\"type\": \"custom\"}, \"extractor1_conv1_bias\": {\"type\": \"custom\"}, \"extractor1_conv2_weight\": {\"type\": \"custom\"}, \"extractor1_conv2_bias\": {\"type\": \"custom\"}, \"extractor2_conv1_weight\": {\"type\": \"custom\"}, \"extractor2_conv1_bias\": {\"type\": \"custom\"}, \"extractor2_conv2_weight\": {\"type\": \"custom\"}, \"extractor2_conv2_bias\": {\"type\": \"custom\"}, \"scale_weights\": {\"type\": \"custom\"}, \"pixel_loss_weight\": {\"type\": \"custom\"}, \"perceptual_loss_weight\": {\"type\": \"custom\"}, \"edit_region_weight_multiplier\": {\"type\": \"custom\"}}, \"tolerance\": {\"max_atol\": 8.562047923987848e-07, \"max_rtol\": 1.1920928955078125e-07, \"required_matched_ratio\": 0.99, \"_provenance\": \"max run-to-run error over 10 seeds x 1.25 margin, floored at torch.float32 epsilon\"}}\n{\"uuid\": \"8ca3b10a-06bd-5dec-a5e5-4f2d4741b